ine/godot/pulls/103416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103416","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103416.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103416.patch","merged_at":"2025-10-01T18:20:12Z"},"body":"Small change to add a button which creates a new AnimationPlayer node to the animation track editor when there is no AnimationPlayer node selected. This uses similar logic to `SceneTreeDock::_do_create`. The idea is just to create a slightly more natural flow when there is no AnimationPlayer node, especially for newer users, but it's also just a bit convenient.\r\n\r\nI think it would be worth following up with a similar change to create a new animation when there are none in the AnimationPlayer, and potentially selecting an AnimationPlayer node automatically when the pane is opened if only one is present in the scene (both of which I'm hoping to look at). Altogether this should make the animation workflow quite easily discoverable and intuitive.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com